WEBVTT

00:00:13.596 --> 00:00:15.596
Brazil presents...

00:00:19.612 --> 00:00:21.612
The land of giants.

00:00:26.012 --> 00:00:27.012
Gary Conway.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.350
No, Madison.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.590
Stephen Erwin.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:39.180
No, Marshall.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.250
In the line.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:59.660
Dr. Young Gaslera, A6.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:08.390
June 12, 1983.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:23.880
Are you listening? This is flight 612 to Tower of London A.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.630
We are in a solar turbulence area interfering with your frequency.

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.460
You may change to alternate range.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:30.970
Come you.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:35.850
Not now.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:01.720
It gets worse every minute.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:06.120
What happened?

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:14.970
I don't know what happened.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:17.680
What a nightmare! What will happen?

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.440
Please, go back to your seats and fasten your seat belts.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.780
I'm sure it's a kind of atmospheric disorder.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.430
Get away from her.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:38.620
I think I'm losing control. Help me.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:50.760
It's in the basement, like a magnet.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.000
Subtitles by the Amara.org community

00:03:21.852 --> 00:03:22.852
I'll take care of it.

00:03:23.068 --> 00:03:25.068
He's completely out of control.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:31.140
Just like me.

00:03:31.788 --> 00:03:33.788
or fear.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:05.250
Yes. Re-entry plan already computed.

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:07.810
Start re-entry.

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:18.580
This is Captain Burton. We are doing the re-entry in London.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.990
Turbulence that has already ended.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:27.700
Here I go suborbital 612 to Tower A of London.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:29.390
We are already in atmosphere.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.040
We are receiving instructions from Pouso.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:40.180
We are still not received.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:54.620
The city is down there and there are no signs.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:03.360
Let's get out of here. There's no way out of this tower.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.540
There's no choice. The force cells are weak.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:13.000
All right, comrade. I just hope to hit a very soft spot.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:37.160
My chair! Help me! And my bag!

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:47.080
Where are they?

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:56.340
This fog of London is the strangest I've ever seen.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:58.580
If it's really London...

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:04.590
Did you hear something from Control-A?

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:08.730
I have the signal tuner on all frequencies and nothing.

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:13.560
And it's not funny. I don't hear the land commissioners knocking on the door.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:16.380
I think we'd better go outside and see where we are.

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:21.280
Have a good time until we come back.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.750
What's going on? Where are we?

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:49.340
Don't worry. We made a forced landing in the vicinity of London.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:55.050
For now, they want to stay in their places and tighten their belts.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:57.080
Miss?

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:57.680
Yes?

00:06:57.910 --> 00:06:59.340
Do you want to help me with that?

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.040
But of course.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:02.000
Thank you.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:06.070
I was thinking what would happen if my cousins didn't wait for me.

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:06.990
Do you think they'll go?

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:08.040
Oh, yes.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.180
But if they don't, I'll take him to my house.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.480
And he'll never be an orphan again.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:16.560
Look, you don't have to worry about me anymore.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.000
I'll get off right here.

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:20.600
I'm sorry, Commander, but no one can leave the ship now.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:22.990
Why don't you sit down and rest?

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:25.940
Look...

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:26.720
Don't touch this!

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:35.170
Yes, Miss. We can't be too far.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:39.930
And if I could get a phone call, I'd call my pilot and he'd pick me up here.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:41.750
Oh, I think that's impossible.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.670
However, proper transportation will be arranged for everyone as soon as possible.

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:53.180
For me, it's not enough. A business of 50 million in London that doesn't wait.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.300
Oh, I'm sorry, Mr. Wilson. We're doing the best we can.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:59.190
Call your captain here. I want to know what's going on.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.260
The mission is out of the ship at the moment.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.180
It was to arrange the transfer.

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:04.860
But it will return as soon as they make some useful contact.

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.360
Put on your seat belts. Let's take off.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.100
Where are we going?

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:12.260
Far away. That's my destiny.

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:14.820
What? Where are we going?

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:19.270
What's going on? Why are we taking off?

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.850
There's something out there. I hope you haven't seen us.

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:23.070
What?

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:31.900
Thank you.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:32.760
We're 2,000 meters away.

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:35.330
2,000 meters and there are still buildings around us!

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:38.560
It can't be! This can't be!

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:44.560
Go up! Go up!

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:51.430
What are you doing? We can't go down!

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:54.140
Beck, go back there and watch the well.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.790
We can't go back to orbit.

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:59.960
Look for yourself. We don't have the strength to...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:11.340
to recharge the cells of force.

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:14.910
We need a lot of thrust to reach the speed of escape.

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:17.330
What do you think we have of escape?

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.190
What will the passengers say?

00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:05.970
24 hours, must be playing.

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:09.570
I have to be in London when the Bank of England opens this morning.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:10.810
I'm sorry, Mr. Wilson.

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:12.420
Well, I don't care.

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:15.260
Well, let's be frank.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:17.880
What do you want?

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:20.410
I want.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:22.900
You heard me. How much is it?

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:26.310
What they pay you to delay my arrival in London and I pay more.

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:27.640
No one is paying.

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:29.610
What I said is true?

00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:31.370
Spare me the fairy tale.

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:34.260
You know what I'm talking about. We're in the open market.

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:37.270
So what's the price to take me to London in half an hour?

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:39.080
Listen, Captain.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:46.170
Either you take me to London right now, or when we get there, you'll talk to the police.

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:50.880
That's great. Now go back to your seats.

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:55.680
All of you, go back to your seats.

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:05.040
Who told the London Radio about Commander Fitzhag?

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:07.320
It's none of my business if the police look for him.

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:09.390
As long as he doesn't cause trouble for us.

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:11.720
I think they mistrust the wrong man.

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:14.840
He doesn't look like the kind who would steal a million dollars.

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:04.860
But no one should leave the ship.

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:06.420
It was a direct order.

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:09.660
Every sailor or soldier must obey a direct order.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:15.520
I know. Before I died, my father was colonel-tenant of the riflemen.

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:21.060
My young man, you force me to break the act of official trust.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:23.720
But I trust you.

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:26.320
In fact, I'm a secret mail.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:29.720
So why isn't it in your wrist?

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:37.720
You're very smart, but let me tell you that there are terrible men

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:41.080
who would not tell me anything about this.

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:44.500
That's why I have to risk myself here.

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:46.150
I understand, sir.

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:47.780
I knew it, boy.

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:50.970
By the way, for greater security,

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:55.830
I hope that what we talked about remains a secret.

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:56.920
Yes, sir.

00:14:58.030 --> 00:14:58.950
You're a good boy.

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:02.680
Goodbye.

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:44.060
Go away! You're ruining everything!

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:57.410
I'm reaching for you, sir.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:15:58.040
Where?

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:02.550
Go to the other side. Say you didn't see me. Say anything.

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:12.760
Commander Fitzhug and the boy have disappeared.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:14.490
When did you last see them?

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:18.710
A few minutes ago. I went to the kitchen and when I came back they were gone.

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:20.340
See if the others know where they are.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:20.720
Right.

00:16:22.050 --> 00:16:24.100
You can put them to recharge.

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:28.550
I'll turn on the bow lights with full force. Maybe we can see them out there.

00:16:29.490 --> 00:16:29.810
Steve.

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:33.610
This will delay our recharge for at least an hour.

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:47.370
All right, call me. I'll go to the radio.

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:54.460
I have a great idea. I'll go with you.

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:56.460
That won't be necessary.

00:16:57.420 --> 00:16:59.970
Dan, turn off the lights and don't turn them on.

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:03.900
I'll call you every 15 minutes, all right?

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:04.180
Yes.

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:10.390
I need to see what's out there.

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:10.850
Please.

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:29.070
Turn on the radar screen and watch...

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:41.840
Right. Steve, I don't know what's going on, but there's a bit of movement out there.

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:46.510
It looks like someone of our size.

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:50.840
It's kind of hard to calculate. There's a lot of movement in the intersection.

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:00.960
Steve, what's going on?

00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:06.360
Steve, can you hear me?

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:07.680
Something happened.

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:15.120
It's nothing.

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:17.400
What's going on?

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:19.860
Giant spiders.

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:22.780
Hold on, Steve. I'll go get them.

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:36.920
Spiders. Giant spiders.

00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:06.050
Hello. I know what you have to say, but I had to come.

00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:07.490
Go back to the ship. Now.

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:11.570
But alone? Something could happen to me.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.920
I have to try to find Fitzhagel before it's too late.

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:18.150
Too late?

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:19.670
Before something else finds you.

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:22.300
What Captain Barton said, Edward.

00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:27.860
Yes, sir. We'd better go back to the ship.

00:22:32.680 --> 00:22:33.900
Open the door! Open the door!

00:22:37.900 --> 00:22:39.320
We have to get out of here!

00:22:39.480 --> 00:22:47.060
I have to close the door!

00:22:47.060 --> 00:22:48.060
The thing is out there!

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:32.770
I don't want to get out of here!

00:23:35.550 --> 00:23:58.640
Are you all right?

00:24:00.540 --> 00:24:01.020
Yes, very well.

00:24:01.680 --> 00:24:05.600
Dan shot the retro-stabilizers.

00:24:06.140 --> 00:24:09.080
And what can this do? We are lost!

00:24:09.810 --> 00:24:11.270
We are lost!

00:24:13.610 --> 00:24:17.880
I know, I know.

00:24:18.520 --> 00:24:19.630
That mouth!

00:24:30.280 --> 00:24:33.820
If this cat comes near the reactor, it will scare you to death.

00:24:34.140 --> 00:24:43.650
What's that?

00:24:43.950 --> 00:24:45.470
I don't know.

00:25:25.790 --> 00:25:29.420
I'm coming, Dan. I'm coming.

00:25:35.600 --> 00:25:42.020
What a nuisance. Don't mess with him.

00:25:43.040 --> 00:25:45.120
I won't talk to my lawyers.

00:25:45.540 --> 00:25:54.330
I told you not to mess with him.

00:25:54.490 --> 00:25:56.780
Never pay attention to anyone.

00:25:57.040 --> 00:25:57.840
We know that...

00:26:05.820 --> 00:26:05.960
And now?

00:26:06.280 --> 00:26:10.510
Keep calling the ship.

00:26:12.790 --> 00:26:13.690
Calling the ship.

00:26:14.070 --> 00:26:15.030
Answer, ship.

00:26:15.250 --> 00:26:15.990
They're listening to me.

00:26:16.010 --> 00:26:16.490
Answer.

00:26:16.810 --> 00:26:17.870
Answer, ship.

00:27:00.090 --> 00:27:02.010
Your loyalty is very worthy, Mr. Erikson.

00:27:02.110 --> 00:27:06.000
When we return to our world, I will make your heroic intentions be recognized.

00:27:06.780 --> 00:27:10.020
Meanwhile, Mr. Wilson will fix the engines without further delay, right?

00:27:11.810 --> 00:27:15.260
Look, I don't care if he fixes it or not.

00:27:15.970 --> 00:27:19.450
We will not leave here without Captain Barton or Valery Scott.

00:27:20.450 --> 00:27:21.710
I'm being clear now.

00:27:22.010 --> 00:27:28.290
Getting out of the screen.

00:27:29.270 --> 00:27:29.870
I will increase the...

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:30.580
Two kilometers.

00:27:34.680 --> 00:27:34.900
Anything?

00:27:35.480 --> 00:27:40.960
The last answer is right here.

00:27:41.100 --> 00:27:43.250
Small signals.

00:27:54.280 --> 00:27:54.800
Useless.

00:28:00.090 --> 00:28:01.990
This is not a regular weapon, is it, sir?

00:28:05.400 --> 00:28:08.520
Let's say it's part of our equipment.

00:28:13.600 --> 00:28:15.360
A very vital part of our equipment.

00:28:35.500 --> 00:28:36.320
Sir, Professor...

00:30:27.450 --> 00:30:28.650
To find out who we are, maybe you can help us.

00:30:31.240 --> 00:30:32.160
I'm going to talk to him.

00:30:33.610 --> 00:30:34.330
You've lost your mind.

00:30:34.800 --> 00:30:36.240
Don't worry, I'm just going to talk.

00:30:36.480 --> 00:30:38.620
Otherwise, he'll seem civilized.

00:30:39.640 --> 00:30:41.260
For him, we have only three senses.

00:30:42.080 --> 00:30:46.610
Maybe you don't mind a bottle being fed three times a day with a dropper,

00:30:46.670 --> 00:30:47.530
but I don't, thank you.

00:33:30.988 --> 00:33:32.988
Oh

00:34:22.360 --> 00:34:24.040
It's just that it doesn't look like a hook very much.

00:34:24.640 --> 00:34:25.580
But it will work.

00:34:30.870 --> 00:34:37.590
A group of little dwarfs wanting to attack a world of giants with a broken blade and a pin.

00:34:38.290 --> 00:34:43.430
We're going to get Steve Valer Scott.

00:34:43.710 --> 00:34:45.470
Or die in the attempt.

00:34:46.070 --> 00:34:51.260
Look, sir, it's not so bad as you say. We have one more weapon.

00:34:51.380 --> 00:34:52.300
Your equipment.

00:34:52.940 --> 00:34:54.940
Weapon? What weapon?

00:34:55.600 --> 00:34:58.380
The weapon. The one that says we're leaving now.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:05.730
This ship is inoperable.

00:35:05.770 --> 00:35:07.820
If you're here, Mr. Wilson will make it work.

00:35:08.160 --> 00:35:12.000
He's an engineer. He's got the right engines.

00:35:12.300 --> 00:35:13.960
You won't obey him.

00:35:15.320 --> 00:35:17.660
I learned long ago not to argue with a gun.

00:35:18.550 --> 00:35:28.010
Shut up! I'm not bluffing.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:38.080
You want to be a dead hero? I'll shoot, I swear I'll shoot!

00:35:39.130 --> 00:35:41.560
All right, shoot. But what after?

00:35:41.960 --> 00:35:46.020
Can you take this ship out of here? Can any of the others?

00:35:47.840 --> 00:35:51.340
I'll shoot! I'll shoot!

00:36:08.280 --> 00:36:08.640
Wait for me.

00:36:08.840 --> 00:36:28.140
Are you teaching me that I'm nothing?

00:36:28.480 --> 00:36:28.720
No.

00:36:31.310 --> 00:36:35.730
I just thought that since he's the only soldier here, he'd be the first to fight.

00:36:40.400 --> 00:36:45.920
Listen, boy, I swear I've never been a soldier.

00:36:46.320 --> 00:36:58.520
I'm nothing without value.

00:37:00.920 --> 00:37:02.580
that has never been in a war.

00:37:03.980 --> 00:37:07.710
But it could be, sir. It could be.

00:40:04.640 --> 00:40:06.400
I think I can go up there.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:30.180
Oh

00:42:35.240 --> 00:42:35.840
Let's go, let's go.

00:43:30.480 --> 00:43:30.980
Thank you.

00:45:04.120 --> 00:45:04.380
I need to do something!

00:45:04.960 --> 00:45:06.260
I need to...

00:45:43.948 --> 00:45:44.948
Good luck.

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:02.000
You

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:41.430
...the bottom of the barrel, a dump of garbage...

00:47:45.000 --> 00:47:45.920
We'll see if we can get back to the ship.

00:48:30.670 --> 00:48:41.050
The devil is here! Let's go!

00:48:41.110 --> 00:48:42.750
You guys, help!

00:48:45.000 --> 00:48:45.260
Thank you.

00:50:22.400 --> 00:50:29.010
in this hidden world that, never knowing...

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:31.280
What's going to happen now?

00:50:31.468 --> 00:50:32.928
I can't take it!

00:50:33.964 --> 00:50:34.964
I don't want to do it!

00:50:37.100 --> 00:50:39.600
From now on, this is how it will be in this world.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:00.200
Thank you.
